{
  "notes": "Lo-fi, E-flat lydian, 78 BPM, swung sixteenths (62 %). A half-remembered radio: a granular cloud of dusty piano grains (GRAIN LOFI CLOUD, its tone filtered) holding open triads (root, fifth, the tenth on top), so every chord is a slow swell; a mellow phase-distortion bass (CZ BASS, the DCW closed) with a swung push into the third beat and an octave pop; the player's glassy electric piano on the Smart Keys (DX RHODES, the index lowered; major pentatonic, which the lydian fourth never touches); and the VINTAGE rhythm box, soft, with a conga ghost. The master is the static: DUST crackle and hiss, a triplet echo, a wide dark room, the chorus slow. Harmony (triads; the lydian II is the colour): A I II, two bars each; B I iii vi II; C vi II V I, round the fifths (the lift); D iii II, drifting. ENERGY adds the bass, then kick, snare and eighth hats, then the swung ghost hats, the conga, a shaker and fills; it never touches the swing, and the levels give a little back at the top. All material is original.",
